[Music]  three decades of regret eddie murphy  turned down playing a different eddie  and one of disney's greatest cult  classics why he thought the movie was  just too weird  eddie murphy is as iconic as his movies  the actor and comedian is legendary  thanks to films like coming to america  beverly hills cop and shrek but even  though murphy has played some of the  most recognizable roles in hollywood  he's also had the bad luck of playing  some of the worst the actor has been  nominated for nine razzie awards and  managed to take home three thanks in  part to the likes of norbit and the  adventures of pluto nash those flops  didn't exactly help his career but  thanks to coming to america too and  2019's dolomite is my name the actor has  once again entered the limelight what a  totally unexpected surprise  it's almost hard to believe the number  of recognizable roles the actor has to  his name but one more could have been  added to that list what movie does  murphy still regret turning down after  all these years you might be surprised  to learn that it was none other than the  groundbreaking who framed roger rabbit  released in 1988 who framed roger rabbit  is a bold film that seamlessly blends  live action and animation into an  engaging story that still holds up  against modern standards the movie stars  bob hoskins as eddie valiant a private  detective who gets drawn into a murder  investigation involving roger rabbit the  movie was an unmitigated success it  currently holds a 97 on rotten tomatoes  and earned over 154 million dollars  domestically against a 70 million dollar  budget but tell me eddie is that a  rabbit in your pocket you're just happy  to see me  while speaking with jimmy fallon in late  2019 eddie murphy said that he was  offered the starring role of eddie  valiant he passed on the film because  the concept was so unusual that he  didn't think it had any chance of being  a success and i was like  what animation in people that sound like  [ __ ] to me  now every time i see it like  with murphy in the lead role who framed  roger rabbit would have undoubtedly been  a very different movie than the one we  know now but that's just the way the  business goes hollywood is filled with  countless what-if stories actors turn  down roles or back out for various  reasons and as it turns out murphy more  than has his fair share of these stories  in addition to missing out on who framed  roger rabbit murphy most notably lost  the chance to star in 1984's  ghostbusters murphy could have played  winston but he instead opted to star in  beverly hills cop it proved to be a  fruitful move rather than feature as one  person in an ensemble murphy had the  chance to lead a film that went on to  spawn two sequels but that wasn't  necessarily a strategic decision on  murphy's part the actor claimed in an  interview with extra in 2003 that like  roger rabbit he also turned down  ghostbusters because he didn't see the  premise having any chance of success as  he put it at the time quote this sounds  like a crock the actor also passed on  starring as detective carter in the hit  action comedy rush hour to instead star  in the widely forgotten holy man  i guess that's a good way to go  rush hour would spawn several sequels  while holy man was a box office and  critical bomb in an interview with extra  murphy dished on the process with his  usual sense of humor saying it's funny  when i think of it now it was like you  can go jump all over california with  jackie chan or go to miami and wear a  robe for three months i went to miami  and you see the results funnily enough  even though murphy turned down rush hour  he actually inspired the entire film  according to an interview the eventual  rush hour star chris tucker gave to east  coast radio when uh eddie murphy did  beverly hills cop yeah that's that's my  rush hour i wanted to that's why rush  hour came about because because of eddie  murphy's beverly hills cop  but despite missing out on all these  blockbuster movies murphy has still only  claimed to regret turning down who  framed roger rabbit fortunately thanks  to his recent resurgence murphy isn't  hurting for good roles these days all  these years later it's safe to say he's  still got it  yeah you still got it  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

